{"summary":"Fix escaped dollar handling in Substitute","explanation":"The current `SubstituteAndAppendArray` treats `$$` as two output bytes: the sizing pass adds 2, and the write pass emits two dollar characters. That causes `Substitute("$$")` to return `"$$"` instead of the asserted `"$"`, and `Substitute("$$1")` to return `"$$1"` instead of `"$1"`. Count and emit one literal dollar for the escape so the size calculation matches the output; placeholder and invalid-format handling remain unchanged.","edits":[{"path":"absl/strings/substitute.cc","old":"      } else if (format[i + 1] == '$') {
        size += 2;
        ++i;  // Skip next char.","new":"      } else if (format[i + 1] == '$') {
        ++size;
        ++i;  // Skip next char."},{"path":"absl/strings/substitute.cc","old":"            } else if (format[i + 1] == '$') {
              *target++ = '$';
              *target++ = '$';
              ++i;  // Skip next char.","new":"            } else if (format[i + 1] == '$') {
              *target++ = '$';
              ++i;  // Skip next char."}]}
